public int findLargestSubstring(List<String> strings) {
    int longestCommonSubstring = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < strings.size(); i++) {
        for (int j = i + 1; j < strings.size(); j++) {
            int currentSubstring = longestCommonSubstring(strings.get(i), strings.get(j));
            if (currentSubstring > longestCommonSubstring) {
                longestCommonSubstring = currentSubstring;
            }
        }
    }
    return longestCommonSubstring;
}

private int longestCommonSubstring(String str1, String str2) {
    int m = str1.length();
    int n = str2.length();
    int dp[][] = new int[m + 1][n + 1];

    for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {
        for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {
            if (str1.charAt(i - 1) == str2.charAt(j - 1)) {
                dp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j - 1] + 1;
            } else {
                dp[i][j] = 0;
            }
        }
    }

    return dp[m][n];
}
```
This function first finds the longest common substring between every pair of strings in the list, and then returns the largest of these common substrings.
The `longestCommonSubstring` function is a modified version of the function from the longest common substring problem, and it returns the length of the longest common substring between the two given strings.
The function uses a dynamic programming approach, where we build a 2D array `dp` where `dp[i][j]` represents the length of the longest common substring between the first `i` characters of `str1` and the first `j` characters of `str2`.
The `dp` array is filled in using the recurrence relation:
```
dp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j - 1] + 1, if str1[i - 1] == str2[j - 1]
dp[i][j] = 0, otherwise
```
The length of the longest common substring between `str1` and `str2` is returned as `dp[m][n]`, where `m` and `n` are the lengths of `str1` and `str2` respectively.

